  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:qu3fj2ec4tf4diaxu46m57jm/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxtix7e5zc2l",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "AI researchers warn technology 'months away' from being able to connect to wifi using eduroam",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mxtix7e5zc2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-14T12:04:06.145Z",
      "likes": 846,
      "replies": 16,
      "reposts": 216,
      "score": 8.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 3,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 54.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxxj65qhac2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This paper shows why I am skeptical of the idea that frontier models can be easily replaced by cheaper ones (and why you should use the best models as orchestrators): Small improvements in accuracy & judgement compound over long-horizon tasks, creating huge gains in outcomes and reduction in errors.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxxj65qhac2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T02:18:38.285Z",
      "likes": 117,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwf7wo7rs2x",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The sudden collapse of the value of Chain-of-Thought (even summarized CoT) in the agentic era changes working with AI.\n\nEffectively steering AIs and getting any sort of observability now requires you to ask for interim outputs & tests, and to use AI help to troubleshoot problems you find.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxwf7wo7rs2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:35:23.276Z",
      "likes": 58,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 4,
      "score": 6.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 27.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxxjezatj22t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "You may save money in the short term, at the expense of worse work at the end. That doesn't mean small models can't do tons of valuable work, but you want to make sure they are orchestrated and error-checked by larger ones for many kinds of tasks.\n\nPaper: arxiv.org/pdf/2509.09677",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxxjezatj22t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T02:22:28.461Z",
      "likes": 36,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.6,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxzaa6e2yc2h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "1. If you have shoddy cyber sanitation like exposed secrets, AI will find it and use it\n\n2. We really need to be training AI agents to know better.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mxzaa6e2yc2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:01.837Z",
      "likes": 2,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 4.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.8,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 0.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwdd7562c2w",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "Next week I'm speaking on a panel for open access week about AI and scholarly communication, and I'm going to talk about the ACM digital library. Does anyone have examples of e.g. mistakes in AI summaries, particularly ridiculous \"podcast\" things, etc.?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mxwdd7562c2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:01:25.334Z",
      "likes": 4,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 4.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 27.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxyzjfsets2b",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I spoke with CNN on LLM chain-of-thought and why AI labs are having trouble monitoring agents. Final version ended up focusing on the use of shorthand that agents are starting to prefer. It's not the most interesting aspect, imo, but perhaps the easiest to understand.\n\nwww.cnn.com/2026/10/16/t...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mxyzjfsets2b",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T16:43:55.444Z",
      "likes": 4,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwf4huoqs2n",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "This is a panel for open access week about scholarly communication. \n\nI have no idea what models ACM is using - if they're not using the \"newest\" and \"best\" that probably just makes it worse.",
